{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "project-grades-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.60: `project-grades`, a PROJECT-domain run whose on-network links differ in GRADE and two of whose speeds lie outside their road type's drive schedules, computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE plus its PROJECT input database (`inputs/washtenaw-project-grades.esm`). It selects source types 21 (gasoline) and 62 (diesel), road types 4 and 5, running CO and Total Energy, brake wear and tire wear (PM10 and PM2.5).\n\nWHAT IT EXERCISES: LinkOperatingModeDistributionGenerator copies each bracketing schedule at the LINK's grade (java:685-695), so the per-second chain runs once per distinct grade (`projectgrade_rows`, `n_projectGrade` 4: -3, 0, 1.5 and 4 percent) and each location reads its grade's slot (`rsr_gradeOrdinal`); links 1 and 2 have the same road type and speed and differ only in grade. And the out-of-bounds brackets: link 4's 80 mph is above every schedule of road type 4 and link 5's 2 mph below source type 21's on road type 5. CompilationFlags.ALLOW_DRIVE_CYCLE_EXTRAPOLATION is true, so MOVES logs a warning (promoted to RUN_ERROR in a run's log) and brackets the link by the nearest schedule on both sides, factor 0 (java:740-760); the run completes. Before the port the model refused it (`run_linkCountMismatches`, `run_linkGradeMismatches` and `run_bracketsOutOfBounds`).\n\n`n_outputRate` IS 5245. `run_domainUnported` is 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "project-domain"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/project-grades/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0236_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020. The scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
